  "body": "## Summary\nFixes the failing CI on main that generated the GitHub 'run failed' notifications in the last 48h.\n\n## Root causes\n1. `tests.yml` runs `uv run python -m pytest tests` without installing the `mantle2` extra, but `tests/appai/test_terminal.py` imports `mantle` -> **ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'mantle'** on all 4 jobs.\n2. `appai-certification.yml` calls `scripts/demo.sh` directly, but the script was committed with mode `100644` (not executable) -> **exit code 126**.\n\n## Changes\n- `tests/appai/test_terminal.py`: gate the 4 `mantle`-dependent tests behind a `requires_mantle` marker so the plain tests workflow skips them cleanly. They still run and pass in the certification workflow where `mantle-os` is installed (verified: 7/7 pass with mantle, 3 pass + 4 skip without).\n- `pyproject.toml`: add `mantle`/`mantle.*` to mypy `ignore_missing_imports` (mantle-os ships no py.typed stubs; these errors previously blocked the mypy step once pytest was green).\n- `scripts/demo.sh`: set executable bit (`100644` -> `100755`).\n\n## Verification\n- Full suite with mantle installed: 299 passed, 4 skipped.\n- `test_terminal.py` with mantle: 7 passed. Without mantle (simulated): 3 passed, 4 skipped.\n- demo.sh runs to completion.",
